 ## Background
-Standard approaches often require converting unstructured data into tetrahedral or hexahedral elements, which can introduce topological errors or computational overhead [S1]. The Gallagher-Nagtegaal method addresses the visual quality issues of linear interpolation by fitting bicubic patches, while the polyhedral and pentahedral methods extend robustness to complex cell types [S1, 5321-gallagher-nagtegaal-bicubic-method.md].
